[["de11a7fe_8f4eec0f",8,-1,1,"reset?"],["f2472f11_1e339a45",8,-1,1,"This description explains what/how this CL does, but not why. Can you elaborate on the purpose of this change? Is this fixing a wrong behavior in the current implementation, or improving performance?…"],["a6d3e75d_dc4622e5",15,0,0,"(For a follow-up CL) If these maps are keyed with origin, can we use `url::Origin` as the key?"],["beb00412_aa4b9ca8",15,0,0,"Why do we call `reset_on_disconnect()` here?"]],0,201],[7123094,20405,5,0.239,0.194,[[34,0]],[["10f7fd30_fdce4e0e",38,-7,1,"nit: Could you add a bit more context? Something like, \"When enabled, WebView#preconnect will use a connection config for NetworkContext::preconnect (or whatever that method is, can't remember at the…"]],0,202],[7160926,20420,79,2.344,1.853,[[15,23]],[["1cba932d_a87c5451",8,-8,1,"can we also have a link to the crash bug?"],["1879369c_3da233f4",14,-7,1,"I feel like the current flag/param structure is confusing. The feature flag says \"bind every time\" but the param suggests \"bind only on observer event\". To reduce confusion, can we revamp the entire…"],["30015f64_26943d1a",14,-7,1,"Can you add a comment explaining what \"ObserverEvent\" indicates? Or, we could give a more specific name to this param like `kOnlyBindOnConnectionClosedOrFailed`."],["4e828072_2c007d67",8,-1,1,"Please fix this WARNING reported by Spellchecker: \"Connction\" is a possible misspelling of \"Connection\". To bypass Spellchecker, ... \"Connction\" is a possible misspelling of \"Connection\". To bypass…"]],0,203],[7220391,20425,4,0.015,0.004,[[35,0.5,6,2],[36,0.5,2,2]],[],0,204],[7219224,20425,8,0.407,0.29,[[37,0]],[],0,204],[7219225,20425,9,0.407,0.29,[[38,0]],[],0,205],[7220990,20425,2,0.012,0.007,[[35,6]],[],0,206],[7221291,20427,56,1.101,0.895,[[6,0.707,52,40],[4,0.293,14,16]],[["db98eb15_b3a70e54",39,-2,1,"nit: could you please remove GWS if this is not specific to Google services?"]],0,206],[7235462,20430,29,0.662,0.495,[[16,0.417,22,13],[22,0.278,22,8],[33,0.222,7,6],[39,0.083,7,2]],[["3b933953_de8fb4e9",23,0,0,"This looks up `session_key` in the map three times in quick succession! Terribly inefficient, but no need to fix it in this CL."],["dd1a360d_b18b5833",8,0,1,"Nit: It would be good if the CL description said why the observer might be destroyed before the `ConnectionManagementConfig`."]],0,207],[7236469,20430,8,2.625,2.375,[[16,23]],[],0,208],[7140202,20430,23,0.198,0.14,[[0,13]],[],0,209],[7116488,20438,188,3.848,3.085,[[7,0.729,19,136],[24,0.271,2,50]],[["025827de_01d5cd6a",13,-33,0,"`REUSED_EXISTING_PROCESS` will be the process assignment source in multiple cases not only the RPH reuse for the prerender page. If DSEKeepAlive or multiple SRP in the same renderer feature is…"],["274982a3_6512226e",6,-33,1,"IIUC, the code here is trying to query if there was once a prewarm page committed in the renderer process. Maybe it is better to do so in `GWSPageLoadMetricsObserver::OnCommit` rather than…"],["7228f185_749b2da6",6,-33,0,"Another question is that we are using the navigation request and the process when getting and setting the user data. Can we fetch the previous `prewarm_committed` value stored in the user data of the…"],["b60ab3cb_1bbd1abc",40,-28,1,"High-level comment: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/content/public/README.md Regarding the //content/public, we have some strict rules, and here are some rules that this CL is…"],["e93226fc_ef023c39",40,-28,1,"We can still inherit content/public/browser/navigation_handle_user_data.h?"],["39631fb5_30dd58a8",40,-15,1,"Since the user data is now bound to the navigation request and the RPH, the comments need update. Would you explain that the `prewarm_committed_` will be true for the RPH once a prewarm page is…"],["06cf1be7_883e3b6e",40,-12,1,"As discussed above, this class name is also problematic as the prewarm is a concept outside the //content."],["34496c3a_caa1523b",40,-12,1,"also, disallow copy, and so on?"],["41d8de19_799b7d30",40,-12,1,"`DSE` (large capital to be consistent)"],["c05ee38b_d98aff4f",40,-12,1,"`NavigationHandle and`? Also can this be in the private section? I think external users don't need to know this key as they always access the instance via the Get{OrCreate} class method below."],["85b3b9dc_e2e8eded",13,-7,1,"Should this have a suffix 2? (IIUC, you changed the condition to record this only for the renderer-initiated cases.)"]],0,210],[7221292,20439,34,1.101,0.895,[[40,0.514,10,18],[7,0.27,20,9],[4,0.216,15,7]],[],0,211]]}